<Layouts.flash_group flash={@flash} />

<div class="min-h-screen bg-base-200">
  <div class="bg-secondary py-8 text-secondary-content">
    <div class="w-full px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="mb-2 text-3xl font-bold">Selecto without Ecto Schemas</h1>
      <p class="text-secondary-content/85">
        Introspect Northwind directly, run through a named Postgrex connection, and generate the
        complete SelectoComponents LiveView.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="w-full space-y-8 px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="breadcrumbs text-sm">
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/" class="link link-hover">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="/tutorial" class="link link-hover">Ecto Tutorial</a></li>
        <li>Postgrex Tutorial</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <nav class="rounded-lg bg-base-100 p-4 shadow">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">Contents</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm">
        <a href="#scope" class="link link-hover">What “without Ecto” means</a>
        <a href="#dependencies" class="link link-hover">1: Dependencies</a>
        <a href="#connection" class="link link-hover">2: Postgrex connection</a>
        <a href="#generate" class="link link-hover">3: Generate</a>
        <a href="#routes" class="link link-hover">4: Routes</a>
        <a href="#generated-code" class="link link-hover">5: Generated code</a>
        <a href="#verify" class="link link-hover">6: Verify</a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <section id="scope" class="scroll-mt-6 rounded-lg bg-base-100 p-6 shadow">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold">What “without Ecto” means here</h2>
      <p class="text-base-content/75">
        The Northwind sample still uses its existing Repo for migrations and seed data. Selecto
        does not use an Ecto schema or execute through that Repo in this walkthrough: the generator
        reads PostgreSQL catalogs, produces a map-based domain, and the LiveView executes through
        `SelectoNorthwind.Database`.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      id="dependencies"
      class="scroll-mt-6 space-y-4 rounded-lg bg-base-100 p-6 shadow"
    >
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">1) Add the Selecto Packages</h2>
      <p class="text-base-content/75">
        Start after the baseline `mix setup`, then add the four current packages.
      </p>

      <pre><code class="language-elixir" phx-no-curly-interpolation># mix.exs
defp deps do
  [
    # ...existing deps...
    {:selecto, github: "seeken/selecto", branch: "main", override: true},
    {:selecto_db_postgresql, github: "seeken/selecto_db_postgresql", branch: "main", override: true},
    {:selecto_components, github: "seeken/selecto_components", branch: "main", override: true},
    {:selecto_mix, github: "seeken/selecto_mix", branch: "main", only: [:dev, :test], override: true}
  ]
end</code></pre>

      <pre><code class="language-bash">mix deps.get
mix compile
mix selecto.components.integrate
(cd assets && npm install)
mix assets.build</code></pre>

      <div class="space-y-2 rounded-lg border border-info/30 bg-info/10 p-4 text-sm">
        <p>
          `selecto_db_postgresql` owns the PostgreSQL adapter. `selecto_mix` supplies the shared
          generator and is only needed in development and test.
        </p>
        <p>
          The integration task prints the required npm and asset commands; run both before opening
          the generated LiveView.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="connection" class="scroll-mt-6 space-y-4 rounded-lg bg-base-100 p-6 shadow">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">2) Supervise a Named Postgrex Connection</h2>
      <p class="text-base-content/75">
        Reuse the sample app's database settings, but start a separate connection under the name
        that the generated LiveView will use.
      </p>

      <pre><code class="language-elixir" phx-no-curly-interpolation># lib/selecto_northwind/application.ex
def start(_type, _args) do
  postgrex_options =
    Application.fetch_env!(:selecto_northwind, SelectoNorthwind.Repo)
    |> Keyword.take([:hostname, :port, :database, :username, :password])
    |> Keyword.put(:name, SelectoNorthwind.Database)
    |> Keyword.put(:pool_size, 5)

  children = [
    SelectoNorthwindWeb.Telemetry,
    SelectoNorthwind.Repo,
    {Postgrex, postgrex_options},
    {DNSCluster, query: Application.get_env(:selecto_northwind, :dns_cluster_query) || :ignore},
    {Phoenix.PubSub, name: SelectoNorthwind.PubSub},
    SelectoNorthwindWeb.Endpoint
  ]

  Supervisor.start_link(children, strategy: :one_for_one, name: SelectoNorthwind.Supervisor)
end</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section id="generate" class="scroll-mt-6 space-y-4 rounded-lg bg-base-100 p-6 shadow">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">3) Generate the Domain, LiveView, and Saved Views</h2>
      <p class="text-base-content/75">
        One `selecto.gen.domain` call now creates the table-backed domain, overlay, complete
        SelectoComponents LiveView, and PostgreSQL saved-view implementation. Apply its generated
        SQL with the shared setup task afterward.
      </p>

      <pre><code class="language-bash">export DATABASE_URL="postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/selecto_northwind_dev"

mix selecto.gen.domain \
  --adapter postgresql \
  --table products \
  --database-url "$DATABASE_URL" \
  --connection-name SelectoNorthwind.Database \
  --expand \
  --expand-schemas suppliers,categories,order_details \
  --expand-star categories:category_name \
  --expand-star suppliers:company_name \
  --expand-tag tags:name \
  --live \
  --saved-views \
  --path /products_selecto \
  --yes

mix selecto.setup \
  --adapter postgresql \
  --database-url "$DATABASE_URL" \
  --sql-dir priv/sql</code></pre>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-info/30 bg-info/10 p-4 text-sm">
        Keep the database table names plural. `--connection-name` is the runtime process name;
        connection flags such as `--database-url` are used only while generating.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="routes" class="scroll-mt-6 space-y-4 rounded-lg bg-base-100 p-6 shadow">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">4) Install the Generated Routes</h2>
      <p class="text-base-content/75">
        Replace the placeholder Products controller route with the LiveView. Keep the external
        query-contract plugs in a non-aliased scope so Phoenix does not prefix them with
        `SelectoNorthwindWeb`.
      </p>

      <pre><code class="language-elixir" phx-no-curly-interpolation># Inside scope "/", SelectoNorthwindWeb do
live "/products_selecto", ProductLive, :index

# Outside the SelectoNorthwindWeb scope
scope "/" do
  pipe_through :browser

  forward "/products_selecto/query-contract.json",
          SelectoComponents.QueryContract.Plug,
          domain: SelectoNorthwind.SelectoDomains.ProductDomain.domain(),
          domain_id: "product",
          domain_path: "/products_selecto",
          query_contract_url: "/products_selecto/query-contract.json",
          query_guide_url: "/products_selecto/query-guide.md"

  forward "/products_selecto/query-guide.md",
          SelectoComponents.QueryContract.Guide.Plug,
          domain: SelectoNorthwind.SelectoDomains.ProductDomain.domain(),
          domain_id: "product",
          domain_path: "/products_selecto",
          query_contract_url: "/products_selecto/query-contract.json",
          query_guide_url: "/products_selecto/query-guide.md"

  forward "/products_selecto/query-intent/validate",
          SelectoComponents.QueryContract.IntentValidator.Plug,
          domain: SelectoNorthwind.SelectoDomains.ProductDomain.domain(),
          domain_id: "product",
          domain_path: "/products_selecto",
          query_contract_url: "/products_selecto/query-contract.json",
          query_guide_url: "/products_selecto/query-guide.md"
end</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section
      id="generated-code"
      class="scroll-mt-6 space-y-4 rounded-lg bg-base-100 p-6 shadow"
    >
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">5) Check the Generated Boundary</h2>
      <p class="text-base-content/75">
        The generated LiveView already configures Selecto with the named Postgrex connection. You
        should not need to hand-edit it.
      </p>

      <pre><code class="language-elixir" phx-no-curly-interpolation>domain = SelectoNorthwind.SelectoDomains.ProductDomain.domain()
selecto = Selecto.configure(domain, SelectoNorthwind.Database)</code></pre>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-success/30 bg-success/10 p-4 text-sm">
        Generated files to check:
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1">
          <li>- `lib/selecto_northwind/selecto_domains/products_domain.ex`</li>
          <li>- `lib/selecto_northwind/selecto_domains/overlays/products_domain_overlay.ex`</li>
          <li>- `lib/selecto_northwind_web/product_live.ex`</li>
          <li>- `lib/selecto_northwind_web/product_live.html.heex`</li>
          <li>- `lib/selecto_northwind/saved_view_context.ex`</li>
          <li>- `priv/sql/create_saved_views.sql`</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70">
        Put application-specific columns, filters, query members, and other customizations in the
        overlay; regeneration replaces the generated base domain intentionally.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="verify" class="scroll-mt-6 space-y-4 rounded-lg bg-base-100 p-6 shadow">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">6) Compile, Run, and Exercise the UI</h2>

      <pre><code class="language-bash">mix compile --warnings-as-errors
mix test
mix phx.server

# Open the generated UI
open http://localhost:4000/products_selecto

# Inspect the published query contract
curl http://localhost:4000/products_selecto/query-contract.json</code></pre>

      <p class="text-base-content/75">
        Expand the View Controller, choose Detail View, and submit the default four columns. The
        result table should contain Northwind product rows.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Tag join regression check</h3>
      <pre><code class="language-bash">mix run -e 'domain = SelectoNorthwind.SelectoDomains.ProductDomain.domain(); selecto = Selecto.configure(domain, SelectoNorthwind.Database) |> Selecto.select(["id", "tags.name"]); IO.inspect(Selecto.to_sql(selecto))'</code></pre>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-success/30 bg-success/10 p-4 text-sm">
        Expected SQL includes `LEFT JOIN product_tags` and does not include `tag_tags`.
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
